+V64.3.19 EAF-ICER ENGINEERING VALIDATION
+==========================================
+
+Algorithm version: V64.3.19-EAF-ICER-DARM-DBR
+Repository: bdse_v64_3_19_eaf_icer
+
+1) Static / contract
+- python -m compileall -q bdse: PASS
+- bash -n RUN_V64_3_19_EAF_ICER_SCREEN_2GPU.sh: PASS
+- V64.3.19 raw config contract: PASS
+- actual TRAIN-fitted ICER-scalar config contract: PASS
+- actual TRAIN-fitted ICER-dual config contract: PASS
+- B<=16 / M=24 / frozen EAF frontier / frozen utility refinement / frozen one-sided + evidence certificate contracts unchanged
+- residual_beta_uncertainty and residual_epsilon(_cal) remain frozen zero for exact preselection/final-guard admissibility alignment
+- RAER/DALER/DACER/ICER learned arms are mutually exclusive
+- utility-equivalence membership is diagnostic/exact-tie-break context only; it is not a hard ICER gate and not a learned ICER feature
+
+2) V64.3.19 mechanism safety / semantics
+- If raw EAF incumbent is final-guard-admissible, no alternative can replace it unless frozen anchor-support logit > 0 AND direct incumbent-dominance logit > 0.
+- If raw EAF incumbent is guard-inadmissible, deployment incumbent is the DARM anchor and recovery is anchor-relative; this path cannot be counted as direct incumbent-replacement evidence.
+- all-flagged scenes remain fail-closed to the learned operator and are owned by the unchanged structural-risk guard.
+- evidence-certificate failure yields zero ICER learned-admissible alternatives.
+- ICER promotion metrics separately report direct-incumbent replacement and anchor recovery; direct-incumbent precision/capture are the novelty gates.
+- scalar-only and dual-equal-mean policies share exactly the same fitted support/scalar/profile head parameters; only the fixed selection policy differs.
+
+3) TRAIN-only fitter audit
+- frozen support source: V64.3.18 TRAIN-only scalar G-DALER support head
+- support is not refit for V64.3.19 causal isolation/speed
+- reused support has seen all V18 TRAIN; fit report therefore marks support_holdout_independent=false
+- teacher margin appears only in TRAIN-only support/dominance targets and evaluation diagnostics
+- direct dominance target: teacher alternative > max(anchor, guard-admissible frozen raw incumbent)
+- direct dominance objective: unweighted BCE over fixed quadratic evidence-interaction map; zero logit is fixed direct conditional boundary
+- no validation threshold, anchor-logit, mixing-weight, loss-weight, B/M or feature-selection tuning
+- one joint fitter call emits both scalar ablation and dual main configs/reports; local joint-fit validation on uploaded V18 train frontier completed successfully (observed local elapsed 18.35 s)
+- scalar/dual support/scalar-dominance/profile-dominance weight max absolute difference: 0
+
+TRAIN-only design diagnostics (NOT promotion/publication results):
+- ICER-scalar direct dominance AUC: 0.754424
+- ICER-scalar direct incumbent replacement precision: 0.644444
+- ICER-scalar direct incumbent opportunity capture: 0.391892
+- ICER-dual direct dominance AUC: 0.764668
+- ICER-dual direct incumbent replacement precision: 0.648276
+- ICER-dual direct incumbent opportunity capture: 0.423423
+
+4) Runtime / data leakage audit
+- ICER runtime tournament path has no teacher/J_T/future/ground-truth input.
+- teacher_margin / teacher_better are used only by TRAIN-only fitter and evaluation diagnostics.
+- fresh-token selection uses preprocessed-cache scenario-token identity + fixed SHA256 only and does not load NPZ samples.
+- evaluator still verifies scenario tokens after load and --require-all-scenario-tokens remains fail-hard.
+- V64.3.18 inspected fresh unique: 500
+- V64.3.19 validation design exclusion unique: 2700
+- V64.3.18 fresh contained in V64.3.19 exclusion: 500 / 500
+- audited TRAIN unique from frozen frontier edges: 3000
+- TRAIN / V64.3.19 validation-design overlap: 0
+
+5) Speed engineering audit
+V64.3.18 logs show normal extra workload plus major removable cache-I/O duplication:
+- 3000-scene train raw replay: 34m23s
+- 4000-scene validation discovery raw replay: 47m41s
+- each fresh arm evaluated only 500 target scenes but old iteration progress traversed 58,418 cache entries
+- fresh planner latency is only about 0.48-0.55 s/scene, while fresh waves lasted ~27-107 minutes, confirming cache scan/deserialization/cold-I/O dominance
+
+V64.3.19 changes:
+- scenario-token prefilter is moved into PreprocessedBDSEDataset index construction before NPZ deserialization
+- manifest fast path resolves all requested tokens without recursive full-split scan when metadata is complete; conservative disk-union fallback remains for legacy/resumed caches
+- no 3000-scene GPU train raw replay; reuse frozen V18 TRAIN frontier instrumentation
+- no 4000-scene GPU validation-discovery replay; fresh tokens selected by cache identity/hash
+- fresh full replay count reduced from 6 to 4 (raw, frozen V18 profile, ICER scalar, ICER dual)
+- one joint dominance fit emits scalar and dual artifacts; duplicate fit removed
+- launcher records stage wall-time provenance
+- planner-evaluated scenario workload reduces from >=10,000 in V18 screen to 2,000 in V19 screen (80% reduction), before accounting for the larger NPZ prefilter saving
+- no promised wall-time multiplier: actual server speedup remains to be measured by V64.3.19 stage timing provenance
+
+6) Frozen raw planner behavior equivalence
+Deterministic randomized replay against uploaded V64.3.18 raw implementation:
+- cases: 5000
+- error-case differences: 0
+- selected-action differences: 0
+- score-case differences: 0
+- maximum score difference: 0
+Conclusion: V64.3.19 instrumentation/operator additions are exact raw-path no-ops when ICER is disabled.
+
+7) Tests
+- V64.3.6–V64.3.19 targeted regression: 91 passed, 6 warnings
+- full repository: 379 passed, 36 warnings
+- warning classes unchanged: existing PyTorch Transformer nested_tensor / norm_first warnings only
+
+V64.3.19-specific tests cover:
+- supported admissible incumbent preservation without positive dominance
+- replacement only with support-positive + direct-dominance-positive alternative
+- negative anchor-support cannot bypass into an alternative
+- evidence-certificate / all-flagged fail-close
+- fixed quadratic scalar/profile map and signed selected-atom contrast inclusion
+- manifest/token index filtering before NPZ deserialization
+- direct incumbent replacement metrics are separated from anchor recovery metrics
+
+8) Execution safety
+- RUN_V64_3_19_EAF_ICER_SCREEN_2GPU.sh is screen-only.
+- failed screen prints STOP SCREEN and does not run full/test/closed-loop.
+- successful screen only authorizes an independently frozen full-validation reproduction.
+- test/closed-loop remain forbidden until the independent full-val reproduction succeeds.
